findings.proposed_change:
Factor the common boundary continuation into one helper. The minimal core is

```lean
private theorem eqOn_schwarzChristoffelBoundary_of_tendsto (a e : ι → ℝ) (z₀ : UpperHalfPlane)
    {p q : ℝ} {L : ℝ → ℂ}
    (hL : ∀ x ∈ Ioo p q, Tendsto (schwarzChristoffelPrimitive a e z₀)
      (𝓝[upperHalfPlaneSet] (x : ℂ)) (𝓝 (L x))) :
    EqOn (schwarzChristoffelBoundary a e z₀) L (Ioo p q) :=
  fun x hx => schwarzChristoffelBoundary_eq_of_tendsto a e z₀ x (hL x hx)
```

Preferably also package the two Edge existentials once, under the same `ha : ∀ i, e i ≠ 0 → a i ∉ Ioo p q`, as a helper producing a single `L` with `EqOn boundary L (Ioo p q)`, `ContinuousOn L (Ioo p q)`, `InjOn L (Ioo p q)`, `Collinear ℝ (L '' Ioo p q)`, and the increment formula. Proof sketch: take `L₁` from `exists_tendsto_schwarzChristoffelPrimitive_sub_eq` and `L₂` from `exists_tendsto_schwarzChristoffelPrimitive_injOn_collinear`; by the `EqOn` lemma both equal the canonical boundary on `Ioo p q`, hence `L₁ = L₂` there. Keep `L₁` with its continuity and increment formula, and transfer injectivity and collinearity from `L₂` using `InjOn.congr` and `Set.EqOn.image_eq` (both from `Mathlib.Data.Set.Function`). Then under the actual hypotheses `hx : x ∈ Ioo p q`, `hy : y ∈ Ioo p q`:

* `continuousOn_schwarzChristoffelBoundary` becomes `exact hcont.congr hEq` (or derive it from `continuousOn_schwarzChristoffelBoundary_of_exponent_sum_gt_neg_one` and `sum_filter_eq_zero_of_mem_Ioo`, as the `Icc` proof already does at lines 260-267);
* `schwarzChristoffelBoundary_sub_eq` becomes `rw [hEq hx, hEq hy]; exact hsub x hx y hy`;
* `schwarzChristoffelBoundary_injOn` becomes `exact hinj hx hy (by rwa [hEq hx, hEq hy] at hxy)`;
* `collinear_schwarzChristoffelBoundary_image` becomes `rw [Set.EqOn.image_eq hEq]; exact hcol`.
